{
  "case_id": "2011-11-88",
  "document_hash": "82e78068b7d2461d8a206bb27f2a56614072ce47fa892badba8ce516ea87c097",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-11-88",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "82e78068b7d2461d8a206bb27f2a56614072ce47fa892badba8ce516ea87c097",
      "evidence_id": "ev-82e78068b7d2-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nJEFFREY FISHER, ESQ., Stanford, California; for Petitioners.\nLAURA G. FERGUSON, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; for Respondents.\nCURTIS E. GANNON, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeffrey Fisher",
      "case_id": "2011-11-88",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "82e78068b7d2461d8a206bb27f2a56614072ce47fa892badba8ce516ea87c097",
      "evidence_id": "ev-82e78068b7d2-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FISHER: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court:\nUnlike the previous case, this case does not involve the need to formulate Federal common law or to survey customary international law. Here Congress has expressly created the cause of action at issue in a statute. And we know that in every single other Federal tort statute that Congress has ever enacted, it has provided for organizational liability. As, Justice Kennedy, I think you put it earlier, it's a simple concept in our country."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeffrey Fisher",
      "case_id": "2011-11-88",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "82e78068b7d2461d8a206bb27f2a56614072ce47fa892badba8ce516ea87c097",
      "evidence_id": "ev-82e78068b7d2-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FISHER: Thank you. But, of course, the question arises in this case why did Congress use the word \"individual\"? And we think the answer comes from the Tel-Oren case, which is the case, of course, from the D.C. Circuit that gave rise to the TVPA. And in that case, Judge Edwards wrote a lengthy concurrence where he again and again used the word \"individual liability\" and \"individual\" to describe the PLO, which was the very defendant in that case, against the backdrop of international law, which uses the term \"individual\" to differentiate anyone from the state."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2011-11-88",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "82e78068b7d2461d8a206bb27f2a56614072ce47fa892badba8ce516ea87c097",
      "evidence_id": "ev-82e78068b7d2-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Is that -- is that better for you or worse for you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. FISHER",
      "case_id": "2011-11-88",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "82e78068b7d2461d8a206bb27f2a56614072ce47fa892badba8ce516ea87c097",
      "evidence_id": "ev-82e78068b7d2-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FISHER: Exactly. That's our argument."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. FISHER",
      "case_id": "2011-11-88",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "82e78068b7d2461d8a206bb27f2a56614072ce47fa892badba8ce516ea87c097",
      "evidence_id": "ev-82e78068b7d2-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FISHER: Because it's more precise word in international law discourse than the word \"person\" for the reason I described before."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2011-11-88",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "82e78068b7d2461d8a206bb27f2a56614072ce47fa892badba8ce516ea87c097",
      "evidence_id": "ev-82e78068b7d2-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Fisher, one case that you seem to have on your side -- you don't have very many, but you have this one -- is Clinton, which -- which does read \"individual\" in the way that you say and does it in order to avoid an absurd result, what the Court thought of as an absurd result. Do you think that this statute is absurd if not read your way?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2011-11-88",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "82e78068b7d2461d8a206bb27f2a56614072ce47fa892badba8ce516ea87c097",
      "evidence_id": "ev-82e78068b7d2-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Mr. -- Mr. Fisher ended by saying there's no reason Congress would draw this line. Why would they want to hold the individual controlling officers of an organization liable for"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. FERGUSON",
      "case_id": "2011-11-88",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "82e78068b7d2461d8a206bb27f2a56614072ce47fa892badba8ce516ea87c097",
      "evidence_id": "ev-82e78068b7d2-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. FERGUSON: Congress was proceeding very cautiously and incrementally in enacting a statute with extraordinary territorial reach over executive branch opposition."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. FERGUSON",
      "case_id": "2011-11-88",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "82e78068b7d2461d8a206bb27f2a56614072ce47fa892badba8ce516ea87c097",
      "evidence_id": "ev-82e78068b7d2-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. FERGUSON: Congress was focused very much on the Filartiga case, where the Second Circuit had found that there was a norm prohibiting public officials from engaging in torture or extrajudicial killing; and Congress wanted to avoid the scenario where you have a torturer who comes to our shores; and Congress agreed with the Second Circuit in Filartiga that if the torturer comes here, he should not be able to escape accountability from his victim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2011-11-88",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "82e78068b7d2461d8a206bb27f2a56614072ce47fa892badba8ce516ea87c097",
      "evidence_id": "ev-82e78068b7d2-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But the Chief Justice's question was why did Congress do that? What were the reasons for that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2011-11-88",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "82e78068b7d2461d8a206bb27f2a56614072ce47fa892badba8ce516ea87c097",
      "evidence_id": "ev-82e78068b7d2-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: How many judgments under -- I don't know whether it's Filartiga or Filartiga -- that -- that pattern, where the individual torturer is found in a U.S. jurisdiction?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2011-11-88",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "82e78068b7d2461d8a206bb27f2a56614072ce47fa892badba8ce516ea87c097",
      "evidence_id": "ev-82e78068b7d2-0001-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What about the point that the immigration law takes care of that? They wouldn't be able to get into the country."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2011-11-88",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "82e78068b7d2461d8a206bb27f2a56614072ce47fa892badba8ce516ea87c097",
      "evidence_id": "ev-82e78068b7d2-0001-0011",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: You don't have to prove it's an intelligent statute, do you? Maybe it's a stupid statute. Is that possible?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. FERGUSON",
      "case_id": "2011-11-88",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "82e78068b7d2461d8a206bb27f2a56614072ce47fa892badba8ce516ea87c097",
      "evidence_id": "ev-82e78068b7d2-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. FERGUSON: Well, Representative Yatron was the sponsor of both the bill that was marked up where \"person\" was changed to \"individual,\" and then was also the sponsor of the bill that was ultimately enacted. So, he was certainly aware that \"individual\" was selected for this reason of excluding corporations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2011-11-88",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "82e78068b7d2461d8a206bb27f2a56614072ce47fa892badba8ce516ea87c097",
      "evidence_id": "ev-82e78068b7d2-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Mr. Gannon, suppose two people are tortured, and one is an alien who has never been within 10,000 miles of the United States, and the other is a U.S. citizen."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2011-11-88",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "82e78068b7d2461d8a206bb27f2a56614072ce47fa892badba8ce516ea87c097",
      "evidence_id": "ev-82e78068b7d2-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: No, but two victims of torture -- you don't find that to be an incongruous result?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2011-11-88",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "82e78068b7d2461d8a206bb27f2a56614072ce47fa892badba8ce516ea87c097",
      "evidence_id": "ev-82e78068b7d2-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: I'm asking about your position, the position of the United States; not how --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2011-11-88",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "82e78068b7d2461d8a206bb27f2a56614072ce47fa892badba8ce516ea87c097",
      "evidence_id": "ev-82e78068b7d2-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Suppose Mr. Rahim had never been naturalized. I guess that was a mistake."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2011-11-88",
      "confidence": 0.0,
